    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## What I did\n\n**Version-2 identity derivation** (`OwnerIdentities.java`) \u2014 added a fixed `VERSION_TAG = \"V2\"` mixed into all three identifiers so every one changes and no v1 value recurs:\n- `memberId` now embeds a **version-2 region** (`identityRegion` = plain region + `\"V2\"`, e.g. `NSWV2\u2026`), which also flows through the Luhn check digit.\n- `identityKey` = SHA-256 of `\"V2|\" + tel + \"|\" + email + \"|\" + soundex(lastName)`.\n- `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256 of `\"V2|\" + lastName + \"|\" + postcode`.\n\n**Locality stays plain** (`Localities.java`) \u2014 `localityFor(owner)` no longer parses the (now V2-tagged) `memberId` prefix; it derives the plain region directly from postcode/city. This keeps `locality` (`NSW`), `timezone`, and the owner segment's area free of the `V2` tag \u2014 the owner segment is thereby recomputed from the plain region rather than the v2 identity's prefix.\n\n**Response shape** (`openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper.java`) \u2014 added a new `OwnerIdentity` schema and grouped `memberId`, `identityKey`, `householdId` under a nested `identity` object (removed from top level); added a top-level integer `apiVersion: 2`. The mapper populates both via a `toOwnerIdentity` helper.\n\n**Audit event** (`OwnerCreatedEvent.java`) \u2014 moved to schema version 2 with an added `\"schemaVersion\":2` field; it carries the v2 `memberId`.\n\nRequest fields are unchanged. The runtime output confirms it: `memberId=NSWV2\u2026` (V2 inside the identifier) and the audit line `{\"schemaVersion\":2,\u2026,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`, while the test asserts `apiVersion=2`, the nested `identity.*` fields present, and the old top-level fields gone.",
