    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered trace of `POST /api/owners`, read from `owners.POST.yml` and each function class it wires. I've marked each item as **[validation]** (can reject the request) or **[side-effect]** (mutation, persistence, or logging). Everything from `cityCapacity` onward runs under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the whole thing commits once at the end.\n\n## Precondition\n- **[validation]** `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` \u2014 without that role the request is denied (403, via `AuthorizationDeniedException` handler) before any step runs.\n\n## Pipeline (the \"fresh\" create path)\n\n**1. `CheckIdempotencyKey`**\n- **[side-effect]** Reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header and republishes it as an `IdempotencyKey` variable (no DB access).\n- **[validation/branch]** If the key was seen before \u2192 short-circuits to the *replay* branch (`LoadOwnerById` \u2192 `RespondWithOwner`, 200) instead of creating again. Otherwise proceeds *fresh*.\n\n**2. `ValidateOwnerFields`** (the one and only `@RequestBody` binding)\n- **[side-effect]** `OwnerAddress.applyStructured`: normalizes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`), stores them back, and composes the effective flat `address` (structured form preferred over the flat one).\n- **[validation]** Required non-blank fields \u2014 `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone`; all missing ones are collected and reported together \u2192 400 `MissingOwnerFieldsException`.\n- **[side-effect + validation]** `OwnerTelephone.toE164`: strips spaces/dashes/brackets; keeps a leading `+`/country code, else assumes `+61` and drops one leading `0`; requires 8\u201315 digits, and for recognized codes an exact national length (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210) \u2192 else 400 `InvalidTelephoneException`. Normalized E.164 value stored back.\n- **[side-effect + validation]** `OwnerEmail.normalize`: only if email present \u2014 trim, regex-validate, lower-case, and reject disposable/blocklisted domains \u2192 400 `InvalidEmailException`. Normalized value stored back.\n- **[validation]** `OwnerPostcode.validate`: only if postcode present \u2014 must be exactly 4 digits and, for a city with a known region, within that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 else 400 `InvalidPostcodeException`. Stored as given.\n- **[side-effect]** Publishes the validated DTO as a variable for later steps.\n\n**3. `ResolveRegistrationDate`**\n- **[validation]** A supplied registration date later than the server's current date \u2192 400 `FutureRegistrationDateException`.\n- **[side-effect]** Computes the effective date (supplied, else today), rolls weekends/holidays forward to the next business day (`BusinessDay.adjust`), and publishes it as a `LocalDate` variable.\n\n**4. `CheckCityCapacity`**\n- **[validation]** Counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive, via `findAll`); if \u2265 50 \u2192 409 `CityAtCapacityException`.\n\n**5. `CheckDailyOwnerLimit`**\n- **[validation]** Counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the adjusted business day; if \u2265 `DAILY_LIMIT` \u2192 429 `DailyOwnerLimitException`.\n\n**6. `BuildOwner`**\n- **[side-effect]** Maps the DTO to a new `Owner` entity and sets its (adjusted) `registrationDate`; publishes the entity.\n\n**7. `AssignHousehold`**\n- **[side-effect]** Sets `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode` (assigned to every owner).\n\n**8. `AssignMembershipLevelCap`**\n- **[side-effect]** Finds existing non-deleted members with the same `householdId`; if any, stamps their household sizes and sets `membershipLevelCap = max(memberLevel) + 1` (unset when there are none).\n\n**9. `CheckUniqueIdentity`**\n- **[validation]** Unless `sharesHousehold=true` (which bypasses this): computes `identityKey` = SHA-256 of `telephone + email + soundex(lastName)`; an exact match against any existing non-deleted owner \u2192 409 `DuplicateIdentityException`.\n\n**10. `CheckPossibleDuplicate`**\n- **[side-effect]** If `sharesHousehold=true`, sets `possibleDuplicate=false`. Otherwise flags a soft duplicate (same last-name soundex + same postcode, but different `identityKey`): sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` = earliest matching owner's id.\n\n**11. `AssignMemberId`**\n- **[side-effect]** Computes `memberId` (`REGION`+`FY`+`HASH8`+Luhn check digit); if it collides with an existing owner's `memberId`, appends `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 until unique; sets it.\n\n**12. `CountNamesakes`**\n- **[side-effect]** Sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n**13. `FlagBulkSignup`**\n- **[side-effect]** Sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` when more than 80 owners already exist for that business day.\n\n**14. `FlagCapacityWarning`**\n- **[side-effect]** Sets `capacityWarning = true` when the city already holds 40\u201349 owners (approaching the hard cap of 50).\n\n**15. `SaveOwner`**\n- **[side-effect]** `ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 the persistence write (generates the id). A DB constraint violation escalates to the `DataIntegrityViolationException` handler.\n\n**16. `RecordIdempotencyKey`**\n- **[side-effect]** If the request carried a key, records `key \u2192 owner.id` in the in-memory `IdempotencyStore` (so a later repeat replays this owner).\n\n**17. `EnqueueWelcomeNotification`**\n- **[side-effect]** Emits a `NOTIFY` log line with the owner's `id` and `memberId`.\n\n**18. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`**\n- **[side-effect]** `HouseholdMembers.stamp` on the owner; maps to `OwnerDto`; computes the capped `membershipLevel`; writes an `AUDIT` log line and an immutable structured `OwnerCreatedEvent` (incrementing a JVM-wide `EVENT_SEQ`) as JSON.\n- **[side-effect]** Responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the owner body.\n\n## Notes\n- **Validations, in rejection order:** auth role \u2192 required fields \u2192 telephone \u2192 email \u2192 postcode \u2192 future date \u2192 city capacity (409) \u2192 daily limit (429) \u2192 duplicate identity (409). Validation deliberately precedes the load/build so bad input returns 400 before capacity/duplicate checks.\n- `sharesHousehold=true` **bypasses** both the hard duplicate rejection (step 9) and the soft-duplicate flag (step 10).\n- The replay branch (step 1) is the only alternate exit: it loads the previously-created owner under `readonly-transaction` and responds 200, skipping all validation and side-effects below.\n\nI didn't change anything \u2014 this is read-only."
